HST Office: the document tab strip in the HST look (the frame coat's DocumentTabs part), and an accessible
tree for the strip.

- Look (framework/source/uielement/hstdocumenttabcoat.cxx; documenttabbar.cxx only branches to it): the
  strip on the frame surface; the selected tab raised in the raised frame surface with rounded top corners,
  joining the document below; the other tabs flat, a rounded hover behind the one under the mouse; short
  frame dividers between flat tabs; the frame divider along the bottom, open under the selected tab; titles
  in the strip's own font (the body weight; the font size keeps the strip height) and the text colour, cut with an ellipsis only when they do not fit (the tooltip keeps
  the full name); the modified marker a small dot in the text colour. When the strip has to shrink the tabs,
  tabs not selected and not under the mouse give the close button's room to their title and the selected tab
  drops its dot (its cap marks it), so titles keep at least the room of the platform look; hovering a tab shows
  its close button. The close button and "+" draw the icon
  theme's hst-frame/16/tabclose and tabnew glyphs (a vector cross where a theme has none) with a round hover.
  The strip keeps its height (owner decision D8); the platform look, high contrast and
  org.openoffice.Office.HSTAppearance/FrameCoat/DocumentTabs=false keep today's drawing and layout.
- Application identity (D8): the selected tab's top 3 px and a dot before every title in the application's
  mark colour, the new tokens hst::design::AppMark / Palette::aAppMark (Writer, Sheets, Slides, Draw, PDF;
  from the application icons, Draw's amber darkened to 3:1), which replace the colours written in
  documenttabgroup.cxx. Unknown modules take the muted colour.
- Accessibility (both looks; framework/source/uielement/hstdocumenttabaccessible.cxx): the strip is a page
  tab list with one page tab per document (its title, "modified" as the description, selected state,
  a click action that shows it), a "Close Tab" push button in each tab and the "Open in New Tab" button.
  Actions are posted to the main loop and dropped when the strip goes away or its tabs change.
- Tests: CppunitTest_framework_hst_documenttabcoat (marks reach 3:1 in light and dark, module mapping,
  the strip's pixels at 100 and 125 %, hover, glyph fallback, close button size, strip height, the
  accessible tree and its actions).

